  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a small saucepan of water to the boil for the eggs. Bring a medium saucepan of water to the boil for the noodles. Peel and finely grate the ginger (see Kitchen notes). Grate or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Trim and thinly slice the radishes. Thinly slice the avocado.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/135630/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_01-3c5e09c19014ea60abcdf05ac61091d4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Boil eggs: Cook 2 eggs in the pan of boiling water for 7 mins for soft-boiled, or 8 mins for hard-boiled. Drain, then cool in cold water. Peel and quarter the eggs.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/135631/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_02-2926580d9bbc8c56d65fa9aea6b809f9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles: Cook three-quarters of the noodles in the pan of boiling water for 4 mins or until tender. Drain, then rinse under cold running water to prevent the noodles from sticking.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/135632/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_03-a49ec27f5bf99ddf4ba0511d16af9859.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make dressing: Put the ginger, garlic, 2 tbs soy sauce, 1 tbs balsamic vinegar, 1 tbs vegetable oil, 1 tsp honey and half the sesame seeds in a large bowl and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/135633/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_04-bc759d4f4e2c78354fd94ba1a59b85a9.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Add the noodles, radish and spinach leaves to the dressing and toss well to combine. Divide the noodle salad among bowls, top with the avocado and egg, then scatter with the remaining sesame seeds and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/135634/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_05-5a7a1690f603c65ff6737795493d279d.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen notes: Ginger skin can be easily removed with a teaspoon. Simply scrape with a spoon and it will lift straight off.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/135635/photos/large/DNY_Recipe_Card_New_Illustration_HACK-4d24763fbe97269c0089cc30f420a7fa.jpg"
    }
  ]
}
